    {
     "source_record": 1182,
     "rationale": "For macOS applications, code-level and build-pipeline checks can verify hardened runtime, signing, and expected application configuration settings, helping identify insecure development conditions that could make application behavior or configuration more susceptible to malicious plist modification.",
